{"availability":"available","full":"kgtceo/qof-register-builder","name":"qof-register-builder","description":"Builds NHS QOF-style disease registers from SNOMED-coded synthetic records and deterministically flags miscoded free text (with the exact suggested code) and status conflicts — the LLM only drafts the completeness report, verified against the computed results. Demo. FastAPI + Next.js.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-24T08:31:53Z","updated":"2026-07-24T09:36:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://qof-register-builder.vercel.app","topics":["ai","anthropic","clinical-ai","evals","fastapi","healthcare","llm","nextjs","nhs","python","snomed"],"demo":"https://qof-register-builder.kareemghazal.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.618Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.618Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.618Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.618Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A QOF-style disease-register builder + miscoding flagger for a synthetic GP practice. A deterministic engine builds the disease registers from real SNOMED CT codes (per a committed register-definition table) and decides every data-quality flag — free-text problems that exactly match a known SNOMED synonym but carry no code, and concepts recorded both active and resolved. The LLM only drafts the register-completeness report and per-patient correction explanations, behind a deterministic grounding gate: it can never mention a patient id, code, or register that isn't in the computed results.","Built around one idea: measure LLM systems, don't vibe them. In a clinical-coding product the facts — who is on a register, which code is missing — must be decided in code, not by a model. The model's job is the prose; the gate makes sure the prose can't invent facts.","How it works — records → registers → flags → verified report, with the eval harness that measures it:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b445a83ba010a7e115ade51b33f510c939f3bd6b9aabcc83caf6675974cd9a5f","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.771Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:24.771Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A QOF-style disease-register builder + miscoding flagger for a synthetic GP practice. A deterministic engine builds the disease registers from real SNOMED CT codes (per a committed register-definition table) and decides every data-quality flag — free-text problems that exactly match a known SNOMED synonym but carry no code, and concepts recorded both active and resolved. The LLM only drafts the register-completeness report and per-patient correction explanations, behind a deterministic grounding gate: it can never mention a patient id, code, or register that isn't in the computed results.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The deterministic engine, tests and eval gates need no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The engine is the product, so the headline gates need no API key:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Cost / infra: the deterministic engine, the offline tests, and the eval gates need no API key and no spend — only the LLM report calls the Anthropic API (a few cents per run on Sonnet).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b445a83ba010a7e115ade51b33f510c939f3bd6b9aabcc83caf6675974cd9a5f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kgtceo/qof-register-builder/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-0